  - api_clients_description_check: CHECK (description IS NULL OR description = btrim(description) AND length(description) >= 1 AND length(description) <= 500)
  - api_clients_display_name_check: CHECK (display_name = btrim(display_name) AND length(display_name) >= 1 AND length(display_name) <= 100)
  - api_clients_status_check: CHECK (status = ANY (ARRAY['ACTIVE'::text, 'SUSPENDED'::text, 'REVOKED'::text]))
  - api_clients_version_check: CHECK (version > 0)
  PostgreSQL indexes represented by notes because DBML cannot preserve their predicate, expression, or advanced definition exactly:
  - api_clients_management_order_idx: CREATE INDEX api_clients_management_order_idx ON public.api_clients USING btree (updated_at DESC, client_id)
  - api_clients_name_trgm_idx: CREATE INDEX api_clients_name_trgm_idx ON public.api_clients USING gin (lower(display_name) gin_trgm_ops)
  - api_clients_status_order_idx: CREATE INDEX api_clients_status_order_idx ON public.api_clients USING btree (status, updated_at DESC, client_id)
  '''
}

